sequenceDiagram
    actor U as User
    participant C as Client<br/>(React / Swift)
    participant H as FileHandler<br/>(Go API)
    participant FS as FileService
    participant ST as FileStorage
    participant REP as FileRepo
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    U->>C: Choose file and click «Upload»
    C->>H: POST /api/files (multipart)
    H->>FS: Create(uploadedBy, filename, reader)
    FS->>ST: Save(key, reader)
    ST-->>FS: OK
    FS->>REP: Create(File{name, storageKey,<br/>extension, size, uploadedBy})
    REP->>DB: INSERT INTO files (...)
    alt name already taken by this user
        DB-->>REP: unique_violation (files_uploaded_by_name_key)
        REP-->>FS: error
        FS->>FS: retry with "name (n).ext"
        FS->>REP: Create(File{name: deduped, ...})
        REP->>DB: INSERT INTO files (...)
    end
    DB-->>REP: file row (id, version)
    REP-->>FS: File
    FS-->>H: File
    H-->>C: 201 Created { file }
    C-->>U: Show new file in the table

    note over C,H: Large uploads instead use the chunked session<br/>(POST /api/files/uploads → N × PUT .../chunks/{i}<br/>→ POST .../complete), which reassembles the<br/>bytes server-side and calls this same Create.
